    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d541">

                <pb facs="0474" n="358" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg358"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1019.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Blanchard to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 6, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your October 30. General Vaugues, in command of revolutionary forces which have
                    been coming into Port au Prince for the past two days to the number of three
                    thousand, named for Minister for Foreign Affairs in de facto Government,
                    announced his visit yesterday and called immediately thereafter as special
                    delegate of Theodore to give me the most formal assurance that order would be
                    maintained at Port au Prince, of which I told him I took good note.</p>
                <p>General Polynichi still acts as Commandant of Arrondissement and has also given
                    me renewed assurances of his ability to maintain order and that he would call
                    for assistance from the Legation in case of need.</p>
                <p>Theodore, whose arrival has been announced for the past two days, now entering
                    city amid ringing of bells and firing of Presidential salute.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
